+# Veterinarian Search Stays Out of Scope, Filtering by a Shown Attribute Is In
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-9 declined searching for a pet, a visit, or a veterinarian, leaving owners as the only searchable entity. The row was derived from observed absence during the 2026-07-31 bootstrap survey, and its provenance stayed part of the open consultation.
+
+A request to narrow the veterinarian directory to one specialty reads as veterinarian search under the row's wording. The owner decided the row at intake (2026-09-30).
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Keep NG-9 whole.** Decline the specialty filter as veterinarian search. Rejected by the owner.
+2. **Remove NG-9.** Open free-text veterinarian search along with the filter. Rejected by the owner: free-text search stays out of scope.
+3. **Narrow NG-9** (chosen). Free-text veterinarian search stays declined; filtering the directory by an attribute it already shows is in scope.
+
+## Decision
+
+The owner's words: "Non-goal NG-9 is narrowed: free-text veterinarian search stays out of scope, but filtering the directory by an attribute it already shows is in."
+
+NG-9 now declines free-text search for a pet, a visit, or a veterinarian. Narrowing the veterinarian directory by an attribute it already lists is not search under this row. The specialty filter is the first such narrowing.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- The specialty filter proceeds without reopening free-text search.
+- NG-9 leaves the open provenance consultation for veterinarian search; its pet and visit clauses remain provisional.
+- Only attributes the directory already shows qualify. Filtering on anything the directory does not show is a new owner decision.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-9
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed row.
+- [PRD Veterinarian directory](../prd.md#req-vet-003) — the specialty filter the narrowing admits.
