+# Specialty Narrowing Is a Portable, Uncached Repository Query
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+`REQ-VET-003` narrows both veterinarian surfaces to one specialty, matched on the whole name ignoring letter case. The application runs on H2, MySQL, and PostgreSQL. Owner search reaches case-insensitivity through each vendor's column type or collation. PostgreSQL does not provide it, which is a recorded defect of `REQ-OWN-002`.
+
+`VetRepository` caches its reads in the `vets` cache. That cache has no size limit and no eviction. A narrowed read is keyed by a caller-chosen specialty name.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Per-vendor collation.** Change the specialty column type or collation in each schema script. This repeats the owner-search divergence, and the H2-only suite cannot observe a vendor that is missed.
+2. **In-memory filter.** Load every veterinarian and filter in the controller. This puts a matching rule in the web layer and pages in memory.
+3. **Case-insensitive derived query, uncached** (chosen). The repository states the match in the query. The persistence layer lower- or upper-cases both sides on every vendor. The narrowed read skips the vet cache.
+
+## Decision
+
+Narrowing by specialty is a derived repository query that matches the whole specialty name ignoring case. The query is portable: it uses no vendor column type or collation. It returns each veterinarian once. The query only selects which veterinarians appear. Each veterinarian still carries every specialty it holds.
+
+Narrowed reads are not cached. Only the unfiltered reads use the `vets` cache, and their keys are fixed by the application.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- H2, MySQL, and PostgreSQL match specialties the same way. The owner-search case defect is not repeated here.
+- Wrapping the column in a case function stops the database from using the name index. At the recorded size this costs nothing measurable (see § Scale and Load).
+- A request cannot grow the vet cache by naming new specialties.
+- Every narrowed request goes to the database. This is acceptable while the directory stays small.
+- A later case-insensitive match in this project has a precedent to follow instead of a vendor collation.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Requirements:** REQ-VET-003, REQ-VET-004
+
+## References
+
+- [system-design.md § Contracts](../system-design.md#contracts) — the `VetRepository` and `VetController` rows
+- [system-design.md § Scale and Load](../system-design.md#scale-and-load)
+- [system-design.md § Threat Model](../system-design.md#threat-model)
+- [Non-goal ADR: veterinarian search narrowed](2026-09-30-non-goal-narrow-veterinarian-search.md)
